# Front end

## Visual system

Tokens live in `resources/css/keystone.css` `:root`:

- Ink `#141210`, paper `#f5f4f1`, accent forest `#1f6b4a`
- No default “SaaS blue.” Keep charcoal + stone + forest.
- Layout / cards / type / photo overlays: see `ui-aesthetics.mdc`.
- Contrast, focus rings, 44px targets, semantics, reduced motion: see `accessibility.mdc`.
- Labels, input types, button states, `aria-live`: see `conversion-ux.mdc`.

Shared chrome: `resources/views/sections/` (header/footer) and `partials/chat.blade.php`. Header / footer nav use assigned WordPress menus (`App\Support\Navigation`) with the concept page list as fallback. Identity (phone, brand, CTA) comes from Customizer via `App\Support\Identity`.

Fonts are Customizer-driven (`app/customizer.php`, default Inter). Do not hard-code a display serif unless Matt asks.

## Assets

`npm run build` is required. Manifest is `public/build/` and **gitignored**. Missing manifest = white-screen “Vite manifest not found.”

`vite.config.js` `base` is `/wp-content/themes/acreline/public/build/`. If the folder slug changes, update `base` and rebuild.

Identity CSS (`#keystone-identity`) must print **after** `@vite` in `layouts/app.blade.php`. Compiled `keystone.css` `:root` fallbacks (`--tb-*`, `--cta-*`, `--nav-*`) load with the stylesheet and will freeze the top bar / CTA band on ink if they beat the PHP tokens.

## Homepage search

- Form id: `heroSearchForm` (`resources/js/home.js`)
- Query keys: `type`, `price`, `acreage`, `township`
- Listings page reads those params in `resources/js/listings.js` (`fType`, `fPrice`, …)
- Township option **values** are CPT meta (`Cumberland`, `Straban`, `Franklin`); labels are concept towns (North Ridge, Mill Creek, Oak Hollow)

`window.ACRELINE` is composed in `app/View/Composers/App.php` (listings URL, REST, nonce, listing payload). Prefer that over hardcoded `/listings`.

Booking preselect is `?listing_id=` (not `?listing=` — that 404s `/book/` against the listing CPT).

